# Build-context filter for this example's worker image.
#
# Must sit here, at the build-context root, and must be named `.dockerignore`:
# the SDK's tag hash builds a DockerfileIgnore rooted at this file's directory
# and only loads that exact name, so an ignore file anywhere else is silently a
# no-op for the tag. Without it, editing task.py mints a new image tag and
# rebuilds the worker on every run.
#
# NOTE: supplying a .dockerignore REPLACES the SDK's standard ignore patterns,
# so everything to exclude must be listed here.
target
**/target
.git
**/.git
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
# The worker image builds Rust only; excluding Python and docs keeps launcher and
# README edits from invalidating the image tag.
*.py
**/*.py
*.md
**/*.md
.venv
**/.venv
.flyte
**/.flyte
.DS_Store
